sku|a|Next after; succeeding; ensuing; as, the assembly was held on the following day. ; (In the field of a telescope) In the direction from which stars are apparently moving (in consequence of the earth's rotation); as, a small star, north following or south following. In the direction toward which stars appear to move is called preceding.	j:1gpr,29,1;hfg,26,3;ela,18,2;1toh,17,1;1nqi,17,1;zo6,16,5;1ije,13,2;1pc5,13,1;216h,13,1;1lq3,12,2~zo6,16,5;huw,4,5;hfg,26,3;lpn,5,3;if2,10,2;dzy,9,2;ela,18,2;1lq3,12,2;1isl,7,2;r9e,10,2
