sl6|a|Foolish; silly; simple; weak. ; Foolishly tender and loving; weakly indulgent; over-affectionate. ; Affectionate; loving; tender; -- in a good sense; as, a fond mother or wife. ; Loving; much pleased; affectionately regardful, indulgent, or desirous; longing or yearning; -- followed by of (formerly also by on). ; Doted on; regarded with affection. ; Trifling; valued by folly; trivial.	j:18va,113,3~18va,113,3	e:1oar,32,3;2753,31,6~2753,31,6;1oar,32,3
